---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import AppShot from "../components/AppShot.astro";

const repo = "https://github.com/ibrahemid/tessera";
const appStore = "https://apps.apple.com/app/tessera-2fa-authenticator/id6788814172";

const entries = [
  {
    v: "1.2.0",
    date: "CLI 2026-11-20",
    items: [
      "tess 1.2.0 is a CLI release; the Mac app stays at 1.1.0.",
      "Vault format version 2: tess writes it once an account is in the Trash, has a note or a position, or is imported with a note. Tessera 1.1.0 and earlier, the Mac app and tess, refuse to open a version 2 vault, so nothing in it is lost. tess prints a notice when a write raises the version. The vault returns to version 1 once the Trash is empty and no account has a note or a position.",
      "Windows builds for amd64 and arm64. Linux packages in deb, rpm, apk and Arch formats, with completions and man pages.",
      "tess vault remember on Linux (the Secret Service, with the kernel keyring as a fallback) and Windows (Credential Manager).",
      "tess watch adds folder and tag filters, add, edit, pin, a Trash with undo, and a lock after 15 minutes without a key press.",
      "Trash: tess rm moves accounts to the Trash, tess trash lists it and tess restore brings them back. tess trash empty and tess rm --purge delete for good.",
      "New commands: tess note, tess order, tess pin, tess unpin, tess edit, tess dedupe and tess verify. tess code --all prints every account's code and --at the code at a given time; tess show --qr draws the setup link as a QR code.",
      "Backups: tess vault backup writes a dated backup, and with $TESSERA_BACKUP_DIR set every change writes one. tess vault restore replaces the vault with a backup or with vault.json.bak, the file before the last write.",
      "tess vault rekey replaces the vault key, and tess vault passwd now does the same. On a vault shared with the Mac app that removes the app's Touch ID unlock; the app adds it back the next time it is unlocked with the passphrase.",
      "Import keeps folders, tags, notes and pinned state from exports that carry them. --json on tess import, tess show and tess vault status.",
      "On a terminal the clipboard is cleared 30 seconds after a copy; --clear 0 keeps it. tess rename --handle is now --alias.",
      "checksums.txt is signed with keyless cosign, and every file it lists has a build provenance attestation. The install script checks the signature when cosign is installed.",
    ],
    links: [[`${repo}/releases/tag/v1.2.0`, "v1.2.0 release"], [`${repo}/blob/main/docs/CLI-JSON.md`, "JSON output"], ["/vault-format", "vault format"]],
  },
  {
    v: "1.1.0",
    date: "CLI 2026-09-05 · App Store 2026-09-05",
    items: [
      "CLI: tess code copies the code by default and prints the seconds left; tess <handle> is a shortcut; a code with under 4 seconds left waits for the next one; --clear wipes the clipboard after a delay.",
      "CLI: shell completion for account handles, tess add --screen reads a QR off the screen, add and import read stdin with -.",
      "Import, app and CLI: Bitwarden, Proton Authenticator, Ente Auth, andOTP, FreeOTP+, Stratum, 1Password and Apple Passwords exports. An encrypted export is rejected with an error that says where that app's unencrypted export is.",
      "CLI export: --format aegis, 2fas, bitwarden, proton, andotp, apple-csv, or google-migration (Google Authenticator transfer QR codes).",
      "CLI: tess merge --two-way syncs two vaults in a shared folder.",
      "Fix: a malformed otpauth link no longer echoes its secret in the error.",
      "go install builds report the module version in tess --version.",
    ],
    links: [[`${repo}/releases/tag/v1.1.0`, "v1.1.0 release"], [`${repo}/blob/main/docs/TRANSFER.md`, "moving accounts in and out"]],
  },
  {
    v: "1.0.2",
    date: "CLI 2026-08-10 · App Store 2026-08-09",
    items: [
      "App: recovery passphrase in Settings, which adds an argon2id wrap the CLI can open.",
      "App: clipboard contents marked concealed when a code is copied; the window is excluded from screen capture.",
      "CLI: vault hardening, a lock file serializes writes between tess processes, clearer error reporting.",
      "Interop: strict base32, otpauth label and query encoding, HOTP counter bounds; vectors regenerated.",
      "App Store screenshots regenerated.",
    ],
    links: [[`${repo}/releases/tag/v1.0.2`, "v1.0.2 release"], [appStore, "App Store"]],
  },
  {
    v: "1.0.0",
    date: "CLI 2026-07-21 · App Store 2026-07-19",
    items: [
      "First release of tess (Go) and the Mac app (SwiftUI) on one vault format.",
      "TOTP, HOTP and Steam Guard; import from otpauth links, Google Authenticator exports and QR images; encrypted vault with argon2id and Secure Enclave wraps.",
      "CLI: live watch view, --json output, --copy, keychain unlock, vault status, merge and show, account handles with alias.",
      "App: windowed app with Touch ID unlock, on-screen QR scanning, full account edit sheet, shared CLI vault.",
    ],
    links: [[`${repo}/releases/tag/v1.0.0`, "v1.0.0 release"]],
  },
];
---
<Base title="Changelog · Tessera" description="What changed in each Tessera release, app and CLI." current="/changelog">
  <PageHead kicker="Changelog" title="What changed.">
    Releases of the tess CLI and the Mac app. Release files and checksums are on <a href={`${repo}/releases`} rel="noopener">GitHub releases</a>.
    <AppShot slot="media" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 34vw, 80vw" />
  </PageHead>

  <div class="measure log">
    {entries.map((e) => (
      <section class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h2 class="h-sub">{e.v}</h2>
          <p class="text-sm soft mt-1">{e.date}</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 soft">
          {e.items.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm links">
          {e.links.map(([href, label], i) => (
            <>{i > 0 && <span class="faint"> · </span>}<a href={href} rel={href.startsWith("http") ? "noopener" : undefined}>{label}</a></>
          ))}
        </p>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .log { padding-bottom: 6rem; }
  .links a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; }
  .entry { padding-block: 2.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .entry li { padding-left: 1.1rem; position: relative; }
  .entry li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.72em; width: 0.4rem; height: 0.4rem; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--gold); }
</style>
